       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks unsafe, so I need you to confirm it first.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n- **500 mg PO twice or three times daily with meals**, which is a common starting or titration dose.\n\nPlease tell me which dose you want. If 1700 mg three times daily is what you meant, tell me and I'll enter it with a note that you confirmed the dose."
